// Module 5 quiz - Deep Learning for AI Startups
$CATEGORY: $course$/Module 5

::M5 Q1:: What is the main benefit of transfer learning? {
~Removes the need for a test set
~Makes models larger
~Eliminates overfitting entirely
=Needs less data and training time#The pretrained backbone already knows edges, textures and shapes, so you only adapt it with a small dataset.
}

::M5 Q2:: What does freezing a backbone mean? {
=Not updating its weights during training#Frozen layers keep their pretrained weights. Only the unfrozen parts, such as the new head, learn.
~Deleting it
~Training it twice
~Running it on CPU only
}

::M5 Q3:: Why use data augmentation? {
~To shrink the dataset
~To change labels
=To add variety and reduce overfitting#Flips, crops and colour changes create new training examples, so the model cannot just memorize the exact photos.
~To speed up inference
}

::M5 Q4:: What does a confusion matrix show? {
~Training time per epoch
=Which classes are mistaken for which#Rows are true classes and columns are predicted classes, so off-diagonal cells show specific mix-ups.
~GPU memory
~Learning rate history
}

::M5 Q5:: When fine-tuning the whole network, the learning rate should usually be: {
~Very high
~Exactly zero
~Random each step
=Low, so pretrained features are not destroyed#Big steps would overwrite the useful pretrained features. Small steps adjust them gently.
}
